The '''2025 UEFA Super Cup''' was the 50th edition of the [[UEFA Super Cup]], an annual [[association football|football]] match organised by [[UEFA]] and contested by the reigning champions of the top two European club competitions, the [[UEFA Champions League]] and the [[UEFA Europa League]]. It was played at the [[Stadio Friuli]] in [[Udine]], Italy, on 13 August 2025.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://editorial.uefa.com/resources/028f-1b7b5b724b98-2814feaf1416-1000/20240726_circular_2024_44_en.zip |title=Men's international match calendar and access list for the 2025/26 season |number=44/2024 |magazine=UEFA Circular Letter |publisher=Union of European Football Associations|format=ZIP |date=26 July 2024 |access-date=14 August 2024}}</ref> It was contested by French club [[Paris Saint-Germain FC|Paris Saint-Germain]], winners of the [[2024–25 UEFA Champions League]], and English club [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]], winners of the [[2024–25 UEFA Europa League]].

Paris Saint-Germain won the match 4–3 on [[Penalty shoot-out (association football)|penalties]], following a 2–2 draw after 90 minutes, for their first UEFA Super Cup title.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefasupercup/news/029c-1e78fea1755d-998a1f7aec21-1000/ |title=Paris 2-2 Tottenham (4-3 on pens): Champions League holders secure dramatic comeback win in Super Cup |website=UEFA.com |publisher=Union of European Football Associations |date=13 August 2025 |access-date=13 August 2025}}</ref> In doing so, they became the first French club to win the competition. Tottenham became the first club ever to lead by two goals without winning the competition.

